1
00:00:01,918 --> 00:00:08,758
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:17,183
[CHARM] Toni, I'm so jealous of Billy!

3
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,936
Can you believe it?
Ever since college, she's had it all!

4
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,605
She's smart, beautiful,

5
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,233
and now she's getting married.

6
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:26,693
[TONI] And can you believe it?

7
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:29,362
She's marrying her first boyfriend!

8
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,865
- It's so perfect!
- [CHARM SIGHS HAPPILY]

9
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,199
What about us?

10
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:36,995
When will we have a wedding this grand?

11
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,455
- When?
- Soon!

12
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:40,040
- Soon!
- Okay.

13
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:43,293
You two should find
your Prince Charming first.

14
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:46,254
You can't have the chicken
before the egg, right?

15
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:49,674
Listen to Auntie Precious!

16
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,009
What about you?

17
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:54,554
Have you found your Prince Charming yet?
I don't think you've even found an egg.

18
00:00:54,637 --> 00:00:56,931
- [CHUCKLING]
- Here you go. You good?

19
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:57,891
- That's her.
- Auntie!

20
00:00:57,974 --> 00:00:59,934
Can I take off my barong now?

21
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,020
- It's so itchy.
- Not yet, sweetheart.

22
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:03,646
Your sister Billy will be here soon.

23
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:06,066
Wait, where's the groom?

24
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,400
Where's Alvin?

25
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:15,200
[ENGINE REVVING]

26
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:22,165
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

27
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,300
Here comes Billy!

28
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:39,849
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

29
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:57,534
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

30
00:01:59,035 --> 00:02:00,120
[MUSIC FADES]

31
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:01,704
Excuse me.

32
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,832
Is Alvin on his way?

33
00:02:03,915 --> 00:02:04,916
I don't know.

34
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:07,585
Uh, could you…

35
00:02:07,669 --> 00:02:09,921
Could you try calling him?

36
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:12,549
We've been calling him,
but he's not answering.

37
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:14,968
- We don't know where he is.
- How's that possible?

38
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:16,845
You're his sister.
How come you don't know?

39
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:18,555
We really don't know.

40
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:20,473
[PRECIOUS] Unbelievable.

41
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:23,017
[LINE RINGING]

42
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:26,062
Bro, do you know where Alvin is?

43
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:28,231
He's not answering my calls.

44
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:31,359
What?

45
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:37,198
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:46,457
Dude.

47
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,835
Is everything okay?

48
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:53,131
Hey, Annie! Come on,
call your brother already!

49
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:55,466
- [CHARM] Exactly!
- How would we know where he is?

50
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,468
And don't you raise your voice at me.

51
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:59,345
We don't even speak to that jerk anymore.

52
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:03,725
We were also shocked to find out that
he was getting married to some girl.

53
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,977
- Hold on. Let's all calm down.
- "Some girl"?

54
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:07,437
And what do you mean, "some girl"?

55
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,647
- Your brother's the one who isn't here!
- Exactly.

56
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:13,776
Alvin isn't coming.

57
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:17,906
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

58
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:19,073
Sorry.

59
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:24,078
Maybe he's not here because
she really is a nobody.

60
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:25,914
- You witch!
- You too! Come here!

61
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:27,707
- You started it!
- Because it's true!

62
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:28,958
[ANNIE] Ow!

63
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,668
[TONI] And you call yourself a sister?

64
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:33,087
- Hey, hey, hey! Auntie Precious!
- [ARGUMENT CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY]

65
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:35,715
[BILLY] Get down!

66
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:36,841
Get down!

67
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,135
- What are you doing?
- [SLAMS]

68
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,178
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

69
00:03:40,261 --> 00:03:41,221
- Billy!
- [CAR DOOR OPENS]

70
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:43,514
[OVERLAPPING VOICES]

71
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:44,641
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

72
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:46,351
- [CAR ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

73
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:47,769
- [ARGUING INDISTINCTLY]
- Billy?!

74
00:03:47,852 --> 00:03:53,566
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,361
[TIRES SCREECHING]

76
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:58,238
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

77
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,823
Woah! Woah! Woah!

78
00:04:01,407 --> 00:04:03,451
[TIRES SCREECHING]

79
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,871
Dude, stop the car!
Stop! Stop! Stop!

80
00:04:07,872 --> 00:04:09,666
I just need to talk to Alvin.

81
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:13,419
I know that's not all
you're planning to do, Billy.

82
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,462
I know you.

83
00:04:15,838 --> 00:04:16,923
Oh, so you do know.

84
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:18,466
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

85
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:19,759
Oh!

86
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,844
- [INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CAR ENGINE REVVING]

87
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:23,596
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- Billy, someone's there!

88
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,598
- [CAR HORN BLARING]
- [JORDAN] Oh, shit!

89
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

90
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:32,480
- [HORNS BLARING]
- [INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

91
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:34,357
Oh my God!

92
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:38,611
- [GIA] Hurry up, Alvin!
- [ALVIN] All right, all right!

93
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:40,071
- [SCREAMS]
- [ALVIN] Hey!

94
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:44,242
- Hey! Oh my-- Wait.
- Wait. Why didn't you close it?

95
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,868
We almost killed someone!

96
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:47,829
Dude.

97
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,580
Just stop.

98
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,874
You shouldn't be doing this.

99
00:04:52,458 --> 00:04:54,419
Dude! Hello?

100
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,212
We're going to crash.

101
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,756
We're going to crash
if you don't stay quiet!

102
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,634
Do you want to die, huh?

103
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:05,221
I want someone else dead, not me.

104
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,389
[TIRES SCREECHING]

105
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:08,433
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

106
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:13,021
[ALVIN] I'm almost done. Let's go.

107
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:19,736
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

108
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:25,575
Oh no.

109
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:31,372
[CAR ENGINE REVVING]

110
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:32,749
What are you planning to do?

111
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,126
[GIA WHIMPERS]

112
00:05:35,918 --> 00:05:36,919
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

113
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,255
[ENGINE SPUTTERS]

114
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:41,424
- It won't start.
- For crying out loud!

115
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:46,179
[CAR ENGINE ROARING]

116
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:47,555
- We need to go down.
- Huh?

117
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:49,057
- Get out.
- [ENGINE ROARS]

118
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,308
I said get out!

119
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:51,559
- [WHIMPERS] Get out?
- Let's go!

120
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:52,769
What?!

121
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:55,313
- Vin, it won't come off.
- What do you mean?!

122
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,565
- Just try! Why did it have to break now?!
- [GIA] Vin!

123
00:05:57,648 --> 00:05:59,275
This isn't funny.

124
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:02,737
- It won't come off. It's broken!
- All right, all right. I'll do it!

125
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,239
[CAR ENGINE ROARS]

126
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:10,286
[CAR ENGINE ROARS]

127
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:11,746
[JORDAN] Billy, stop it.

128
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:14,665
Billy, that's not funny.

129
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:17,794
[CAR ENGINE ROARS]

130
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:21,756
- [CAR ENGINE REVVING]
- Billy!

131
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:22,673
Billy? Billy!

132
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,050
- Billy!
- Don't interfere!

133
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,010
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,595
- Dude! No!
- Jordan!

135
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:28,513
Billy!

136
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:29,555
[BRAKES SCREECHING]

137
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:35,103
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:42,151
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

139
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:53,955
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:06:54,038 --> 00:06:56,290
The thing I hate most

141
00:06:56,874 --> 00:06:58,417
is a cheater.

142
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:02,672
But you still became one.

143
00:07:07,718 --> 00:07:08,761
Why?

144
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:12,265
Why?!

145
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:16,686
Billy.

146
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:18,855
It's not worth it.

147
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,357
Let's just go.

148
00:07:22,775 --> 00:07:26,696
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

149
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,792
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

150
00:07:40,334 --> 00:07:46,841
- [GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CAR ENGINE REVVING]

151
00:07:50,761 --> 00:07:52,138
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:54,807
[INDISTINCT CHATTER, LAUGHTER]

153
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:01,522
[LAUGHS]

154
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:05,485
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

155
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,028
[BILLY] Wait a minute.

156
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:08,863
Just wait a minute.

157
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:15,953
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:23,961
[MUSIC TURNS SOMBER]

159
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:45,942
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

160
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,823
Are you okay?

161
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,619
Mm-hmm. Of course I am.

162
00:08:56,702 --> 00:08:57,995
Are you okay?

163
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,914
- It's okay to cry.
- Are you okay?

164
00:08:59,997 --> 00:09:02,250
Hey, you can cry!

165
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:05,836
I already cried once because of a man.

166
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:10,967
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,260
That'll be the last one.

168
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:17,181
[BILLY] It's all right!
Let's just have fun.

169
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:22,061
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>Please don't leave us, Dad!</i>

170
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:24,188
[CRYING] <i>Please don't leave.</i>

171
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,440
<i>Please!</i>

172
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:28,317
[KEEPS SOBBING]

173
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:29,986
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>Mommy, please--</i>

174
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:33,239
<i>Don't waste your tears on worthless men.</i>

175
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:35,074
[OLIVE] <i>We don't need him.</i>

176
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:37,577
<i>We can live without him.</i>

177
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:44,166
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:46,419
[CRYING]

179
00:09:49,255 --> 00:09:50,548
[PRECIOUS HALF-SOBS]

180
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:53,050
Why are you crying, Auntie Pres?

181
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:54,552
Were you the one who got left behind?

182
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:56,262
- I don't know why either.
- You're crying a lot.

183
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:57,388
That's enough.

184
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:59,557
Are you the bride?
Put on your veil.

185
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:02,351
[CRYING, CHUCKLING]

186
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,729
[BILLY] It's okay. Let's just have fun.

187
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,105
It's all right.

188
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:11,527
Go ahead, Auntie Pres.
I'll join you later.

189
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:14,322
Okay.

190
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:17,033
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES FAINTLY]
- [BILLY] Mm! Mm!

191
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:20,244
Auntie Pres, that's enough.
No more tears.

192
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,829
[PRECIOUS] Fine, all right.

193
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:24,749
- My dude.
- Mm-hmm?

194
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:26,500
May I have this dance?

195
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:30,463
- [IN BRITISH ACCENT] Of course.
- Of course.

196
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:31,797
[GIGGLES]

197
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:42,975
["KULIMLIM" BY ANGELA KEN PLAYING]

198
00:10:44,268 --> 00:10:45,728
When are you returning to Australia?

199
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:48,314
Tomorrow.

200
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:50,650
We'll have our midterm exams.

201
00:10:50,733 --> 00:10:52,443
Don't waste your scholarship.

202
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:53,944
Exactly.

203
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,279
It's my last year.

204
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:58,282
Sorry you wasted your airfare.

205
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,243
It's not a waste.
What are you even saying?

206
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:04,080
I'm glad I went home.

207
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,874
If I'm not here,
who's gonna be by your side?

208
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:14,965
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

209
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:36,320
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

210
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:43,369
Hey, you know
I'm always here for you, right?

211
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:46,414
As you should be.

212
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,458
And…

213
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:50,835
he's an idiot.

214
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,003
Alvin's really a jerk.

215
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:54,713
He's a huge jerk.

216
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,674
- Really.
- Really.

217
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:58,384
And, to be honest,

218
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:00,719
you weren't a good match.

219
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,181
Why are you just telling me this now?

220
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:05,808
Would you have listened?

221
00:12:07,309 --> 00:12:08,686
Do you ever listen to me?

222
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:15,067
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

223
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:17,194
Thank you.

224
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:24,994
I got you.

225
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:36,213
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

226
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:45,764
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

227
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:25,679
You crashed into my car!

228
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,556
- You just suddenly turned!
- Huh?

229
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,725
Do you even know how to drive?
Look at what you did!

230
00:13:29,808 --> 00:13:31,185
[MAN 1] You suddenly cut me off!

231
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:33,521
- I was doing fine.
- [MAN 2] Why didn't you move?

232
00:13:33,604 --> 00:13:35,397
Look, I was in the right lane!

233
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:37,441
- I was on my way!
- Look at the damage you caused!

234
00:13:37,525 --> 00:13:40,152
[MAN 1] Yes, that's your fault!

235
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:47,076
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:50,955
[MOTORCYCLE APPROACHING]

237
00:13:51,038 --> 00:13:53,165
- Oop, oop! Okay.
- Good afternoon, ma'am!

238
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:54,959
Good afternoon!

239
00:13:57,836 --> 00:14:00,965
Thank you so much!

240
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:01,966
Here you go.

241
00:14:02,049 --> 00:14:03,717
- Thank you, ma'am!
- Take care on your way home.

242
00:14:03,801 --> 00:14:04,802
Will do, thanks.

243
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:07,054
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

244
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,265
Sir, it's 5:00 p.m. already!

245
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:11,308
Our guests are arriving by 5:30!

246
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:13,686
The LED and stage setup have
been delayed by two hours.

247
00:14:13,769 --> 00:14:15,187
What's the plan now?

248
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,772
"What's the plan?" You're so stubborn!

249
00:14:16,855 --> 00:14:18,107
What do you want me to do, huh?

250
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:19,733
I already said it got stuck in traffic!

251
00:14:19,817 --> 00:14:20,734
It's also Friday today.

252
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:25,030
But if…

253
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,324
you give me your number,

254
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:29,034
I'll make them hurry for you.

255
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,327
Pervert!

256
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:33,330
If my boss comes here
