00:25:29,736 --> 00:25:32,697
C'mon, just a smile?
Or maybe you want a kiss instead.

502
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,866
Please? [SMOOCHES]

503
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:36,368
Fine!

504
00:25:36,451 --> 00:25:38,453
- I'm smiling. Let's eat, c'mon.
- Okay.

505
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:56,179
[THUNDER ROARS]

506
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:58,306
[HEAVY THUD]

507
00:25:58,890 --> 00:26:00,475
Oliver?

508
00:26:00,558 --> 00:26:05,772
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

509
00:26:05,855 --> 00:26:07,357
[THUNDER ROARS]

510
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:08,483
Oliver.

511
00:26:09,359 --> 00:26:10,402
Oliver?

512
00:26:12,654 --> 00:26:13,863
Oliver?

513
00:26:16,825 --> 00:26:18,410
Oliver?

514
00:26:18,493 --> 00:26:20,412
Oliver? I'm here!

515
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:22,122
Can you hear me, Oliver?

516
00:26:22,872 --> 00:26:25,000
- [BREATHING SHAKILY]
- [THUNDER ROARS]

517
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:26,584
Oliver?

518
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:30,213
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

519
00:26:30,297 --> 00:26:31,423
Oliver?

520
00:26:31,506 --> 00:26:32,674
Wake up!

521
00:26:32,757 --> 00:26:34,259
Oliver!

522
00:26:36,720 --> 00:26:37,971
[CRYING] Oliver!

523
00:26:38,054 --> 00:26:40,473
We're going to the hospital, okay?

524
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:43,393
Don't close your eyes, Oliver.

525
00:26:46,396 --> 00:26:47,480
Oliver?

526
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:49,858
Oliver!

527
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:51,318
Can you hear me?

528
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:54,154
Just hold on, okay? We're almost there.

529
00:26:54,237 --> 00:27:00,535
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

530
00:27:01,911 --> 00:27:03,997
[CAR ENGINE HUMS]

531
00:27:14,507 --> 00:27:16,259
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [THUDS]

532
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:22,474
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

533
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:33,818
Ma'am, stay here.

534
00:27:34,819 --> 00:27:40,325
[WOMAN GRUNTING]

535
00:27:40,408 --> 00:27:43,286
[SCREAMS IN PAIN]

536
00:27:43,828 --> 00:27:45,997
[YOUNG BILLY PANTING]

537
00:27:46,081 --> 00:27:47,415
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

538
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:49,709
<i>Take good care of your brother.</i>

539
00:27:49,793 --> 00:27:52,253
<i>M-Ma, why are you saying that?</i>

540
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:53,838
<i>You're smart.</i>

541
00:27:53,922 --> 00:27:55,131
<i>You're a bright kid.</i>

542
00:27:55,215 --> 00:27:56,383
<i>You're brave.</i>

543
00:27:56,466 --> 00:27:58,676
<i>Ma, I'm not brave.</i>

544
00:27:59,636 --> 00:28:01,679
<i>- Ma…</i>
<i>- You'll get through this.</i>

545
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:04,224
[SOBS]<i> Ma, I can't!</i>

546
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:06,267
<i>Don't leave me, Ma.</i>

547
00:28:06,351 --> 00:28:09,521
- [OLIVE GROANING]
- [YOUNG BILLY SOBBING]

548
00:28:11,314 --> 00:28:14,150
[YOUNG BILLY SNIFFLES, SOBS] <i>Ma…</i>

549
00:28:16,611 --> 00:28:18,154
<i>- Ma!</i>
<i>- You're not allowed here, dear.</i>

550
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:19,656
<i>Ma!</i>

551
00:28:19,739 --> 00:28:21,449
<i>Ma!</i>

552
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:23,326
- [DOCTOR] <i>Ma'am?</i>
- [YOUNG BILLY WAILING] <i>Ma!</i>

553
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:26,037
- [DOCTOR]<i> Time of death…</i>
<i>- Ma!</i>

554
00:28:26,704 --> 00:28:28,415
<i>Mama!</i>

555
00:28:29,165 --> 00:28:33,294
<i>- Ma! Please! Ma!</i>
- [DOCTOR] <i>Time of death, 2:05.</i>

556
00:28:34,504 --> 00:28:37,465
[BREATHING SHAKILY]

557
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:39,968
[YOUNG BILLY WAILING] <i>Ma!</i>

558
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:45,473
[YOUNG BILLY WAILING] <i>Ma!</i>

559
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:48,893
[YOUNG BILLY WAILING] <i>Ma!</i>

560
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:51,146
<i>Where's your dad, dear?</i>

561
00:28:51,229 --> 00:28:52,272
<i>He's gone.</i>

562
00:28:53,857 --> 00:28:55,775
<i>My father is dead.</i>

563
00:28:55,859 --> 00:29:00,864
[BABY CRYING]

564
00:29:00,947 --> 00:29:03,074
Doc, let's administer…

565
00:29:03,658 --> 00:29:04,617
Okay.

566
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:07,746
Can you move your toes, Oliver?

567
00:29:12,792 --> 00:29:13,960
[VOICE BREAKING] Okay.

568
00:29:16,379 --> 00:29:17,422
Okay.

569
00:29:20,341 --> 00:29:21,801
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

570
00:29:23,344 --> 00:29:24,262
[SNIFFLES]

571
00:29:24,345 --> 00:29:25,638
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

572
00:29:25,722 --> 00:29:30,935
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

573
00:29:31,019 --> 00:29:32,145
[MUFFLED SOBS]

574
00:29:33,563 --> 00:29:34,773
[SNIFFLES]

575
00:29:36,441 --> 00:29:37,609
[SIGHS]

576
00:29:42,989 --> 00:29:44,073
[SNIFFLES]

577
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:49,204
[MUSIC TURNS GENTLE]

578
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:52,707
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

579
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,292
[YOUNG BILLY SOBBING]

580
00:29:54,375 --> 00:29:58,213
[BABY COOING]

581
00:30:02,759 --> 00:30:04,427
<i>Why are you alone?</i>

582
00:30:04,928 --> 00:30:06,513
<i>Where's your mom?</i>

583
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:08,848
<i>My mother just died.</i>

584
00:30:10,016 --> 00:30:11,935
<i>My father left us.</i>

585
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:13,853
<i>We have no relatives.</i>

586
00:30:13,937 --> 00:30:16,064
[YOUNG BILLY SOBS]

587
00:30:16,147 --> 00:30:18,107
<i>It's just my baby brother and me.</i>

588
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:20,985
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>We're the same then.</i>

589
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:22,153
[SNIFFLES]

590
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:24,405
<i>Mommy just died.</i>

591
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:27,492
<i>Dad left us with Grandpa.</i>

592
00:30:28,159 --> 00:30:29,702
<i>My name is Jordan.</i>

593
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:31,079
<i>Billy.</i>

594
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:40,129
[BOTH SNIFFLING, SOBBING]

595
00:30:40,213 --> 00:30:43,091
<i>I don't know what to do.</i>

596
00:30:45,343 --> 00:30:49,931
[SNIFFLES, SOBS]

597
00:30:50,014 --> 00:30:51,975
<i>There are people who want to take us.</i>

598
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:57,313
<i>They'll separate my brother and me.</i>

599
00:30:58,106 --> 00:30:58,982
[SNIFFLES]

600
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:01,025
<i>I don't want that.</i>

601
00:31:01,818 --> 00:31:02,735
[SNIFFLES]

602
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,988
<i>I won't let them do that.</i>

603
00:31:05,071 --> 00:31:06,573
<i>I won't let them do that.</i>

604
00:31:07,282 --> 00:31:09,325
[YOUNG BILLY CRYING]

605
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:12,078
<i>I won't.</i>

606
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:14,080
<i>No way!</i>

607
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:21,004
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

608
00:31:22,297 --> 00:31:24,716
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

609
00:31:39,647 --> 00:31:45,904
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

610
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:48,031
- [BIRDS CHIRPING]
- [MUSIC FADES]

611
00:31:48,114 --> 00:31:52,076
Diabetes is really a traitor,
especially at Oliver's age.

612
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,953
He's going through puberty

613
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:56,539
and his body is experiencing
hormonal changes.

614
00:31:56,623 --> 00:32:00,043
His patch should be replaced
as much as possible.

615
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:03,463
Hmm, you heard that?

616
00:32:03,546 --> 00:32:06,716
If it's time to change your patch,

617
00:32:06,799 --> 00:32:09,469
you can't say,
"Give me five minutes," hmm?

618
00:32:09,552 --> 00:32:10,720
I'm sorry, Billy.

619
00:32:11,554 --> 00:32:12,597
I'm sorry, Doc.

620
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:15,224
I've told you everything
you should take note of.

621
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:16,517
- You know what to do.
- Yes.

622
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:18,519
- Yes. Doc, thank you so much.
- Okay?

623
00:32:18,603 --> 00:32:19,646
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Doc.

624
00:32:19,729 --> 00:32:20,980
- All right.
- Thank you.

625
00:32:21,564 --> 00:32:23,316
- Thanks.
- Hmm…

626
00:32:23,399 --> 00:32:24,484
- Heard that?
- Naughty.

627
00:32:24,567 --> 00:32:26,152
- Good morning, Ms. Billy.
- Hello.

628
00:32:26,235 --> 00:32:30,114
This is the new prescription
for Oliver's adjusted doses.

629
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:31,199
Okay.

630
00:32:31,866 --> 00:32:34,661
Oh, ma'am! Aren't you the CEO of LoveList?

631
00:32:34,744 --> 00:32:35,995
Oh!

632
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:38,456
Here.

633
00:32:39,916 --> 00:32:42,335
I've matched with someone
who's my type this month.

634
00:32:42,418 --> 00:32:43,419
- Ooh.
- At first,

635
00:32:43,503 --> 00:32:45,171
I wasn't sure if I'd go on with it.

636
00:32:45,254 --> 00:32:47,340
Luckily, LoveList has a special feature.

637
00:32:47,423 --> 00:32:48,341
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

638
00:32:48,424 --> 00:32:49,342
LoveSpeak.

639
00:32:49,425 --> 00:32:50,969
Exactly, ma'am. LoveSpeak.

640
00:32:51,052 --> 00:32:52,804
I got to know Bryan better.

641
00:32:53,554 --> 00:32:56,808
I was convinced by LoveList's
community's comments,

642
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:58,893
so yeah, we'll have our fifth date later.

643
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:00,395
- Wow.
- Wow! [CLAPS]

644
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:01,437
Congrats.

645
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:02,605
Happy for you.

646
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:04,649
Thank you, ma'am, sir.

647
00:33:04,732 --> 00:33:07,568
If you need anything for your son,
just look for me.

648
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:08,903
I will assist you and Daddy.

649
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:10,446
Oh, no. He's not the daddy.

650
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:12,115
- No, no, no.
- Me?

651
00:33:12,198 --> 00:33:15,910
- Oliver is Billy's brother.
- Hey, son.

652
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:18,121
So, he's not the daddy.
He's her best friend.

653
00:33:18,204 --> 00:33:19,580
- Right?
- He's adopted.

654
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:21,457
That nurse was ridiculous.

655
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:24,419
I stayed up late for just one night,
but I already look like a mother?

656
00:33:24,502 --> 00:33:27,797
Ah! It seems true.

657
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:29,382
- Is that so?
- Right?

658
00:33:29,465 --> 00:33:31,467
- Don't forget-- Thank you, sir.
- Anytime, ma'am.

659
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:33,428
She also mistook you for Oliver's father!

660
00:33:33,511 --> 00:33:34,887
- Yes, Daddy?
- Door.

661
00:33:35,513 --> 00:33:38,766
Well, someday, I will become a father.

662
00:33:39,726 --> 00:33:41,436
- Be careful.
- [GUARD] All right.

663
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:43,312
- Thank you! Here.
- [GUARD] Take care.

664
00:33:43,396 --> 00:33:45,565
- Thank you.
- What do you mean, you'll become a father?

665
00:33:45,648 --> 00:33:47,775
Are you ready for that?

666
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:50,069
Have you even proposed to Valerie?

667
00:33:50,153 --> 00:33:51,487
- Propose?
- Yes!

668
00:33:51,571 --> 00:33:53,948
- Not yet, Auntie Pres.
- [PRECIOUS] Mm-hmm.

669
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:54,991
[JORDAN] I'm not yet ready.

670
00:33:55,575 --> 00:33:57,452
But, of course, someday, I'd like to.

671
00:33:57,994 --> 00:33:59,704
I want to have my own family.

672
00:33:59,787 --> 00:34:03,207
But first, there have to be
more branches of the bar.

673
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:04,375
Of course, there's Grandpa.

674
00:34:05,376 --> 00:34:07,253
I want to upgrade his facilities.

675
00:34:07,336 --> 00:34:08,755
- Mm-hmm.
- I need to save.

676
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:11,382
- That's right. That's right.
- I want to make music-- Wait.

677
00:34:11,466 --> 00:34:13,926
Why me? Billy should get a family first.

678
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:16,846
- Me? Shouldn't it be Auntie Pres first?
- [PRECIOUS] He's right.

679
00:34:16,929 --> 00:34:17,764
Oh, yeah.

680
00:34:17,847 --> 00:34:19,807
Thank you so much
for that wonderful question.

681
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:22,477
I believe I don't need a man.

682
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:24,604
- No offense, okay?
- Ouch.

683
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:26,856
Lots of people at
Angels of Grace already love me.

684
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:29,901
And you're here too,
so I'm okay. I'm fine.

685
00:34:29,984 --> 00:34:30,860
Wow!

686
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:34,322
Thank you so much for that wonderful
answer, candidate number 1.

687
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:37,658
Well? Are you coming with us?

688
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,994
- No, it's out of the way.
- Okay.

689
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:44,040
I'll just take a taxi,
so this naughty kid can rest.

690
00:34:44,123 --> 00:34:44,957
[BILLY] Mm!

691
00:34:45,041 --> 00:34:47,001
- All right, all right, okay.
- All right.

692
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:49,128
Thank you,
and sorry for the inconvenience.

693
00:34:49,212 --> 00:34:51,255
- It's fine.
- I thought I'd be late.

694
00:34:51,339 --> 00:34:52,465
Take care.

695
00:34:54,884 --> 00:34:57,428
Thank you. I'll make it up to you.

696
00:34:57,512 --> 00:34:59,055
I'm free anytime so long as it's you.

697
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:03,476
- I'm good with three bottles.
- That's it?

698
00:35:03,559 --> 00:35:05,478
[CHUCKLING]

699
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:10,149
How's Oliver? Is he okay?

700
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:12,777
[BILLY] Oh, yes! He's okay now. Thank you.

701
00:35:12,860 --> 00:35:13,945
[JORDAN] Val!

702
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:16,989
Why'd you come here?
This is a long way from your condo.

703
00:35:17,073 --> 00:35:18,407
Just because!

704
00:35:19,158 --> 00:35:21,369
I saw your message this morning.

705
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:24,831
I was going to jog around the oval,
and that's near here,

706
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:26,999
so I thought of coming by.

707
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:28,417
Thanks, babe.

708
00:35:28,501 --> 00:35:29,627
Billy!

709
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:33,256
- Be careful driving, okay?
- [BILLY] Yes, thank you. Bye!

710
00:35:33,339 --> 00:35:35,383
- [JORDAN] Wear your seat belt.
- [BILLY] Yes. Bye.

711
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:36,384
[JORDAN] Auntie Pres.

712
00:35:36,467 --> 00:35:39,262
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

713
00:35:39,345 --> 00:35:44,183
["SUGAL" BY BRYAN CHONG PLAYING]

714
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:47,395
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

715
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:48,604
Thank you.

716
00:35:48,688 --> 00:35:55,444
["SUGAL" CONTINUES]

717
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:17,425
["SUGAL" CONTINUES]

718
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:29,103
[ROBBIE] Who's Bryan Chong?
He has a nice voice!

719
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:34,066
I heard him sing at a party.
He's from Cebu.

720
00:36:34,650 --> 00:36:38,613
He doesn't know anyone here,
so I want to help him.

721
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:39,822
I mean, he's great!

722
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:46,662
["SUGAL" CONTINUES]

723
00:36:50,917 --> 00:36:52,335
Waiter!

724
00:36:52,418 --> 00:36:53,502
Quick.

725
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:56,172
Yes, sir?

726
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:58,633
There's a strand of hair in your <i>sisig.</i>

727
00:36:58,716 --> 00:37:01,886
I'm sorry, but we wear hairnets
in the kitchen.

728
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:04,513
Hey! Are you calling me a liar?

729
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,849
[JORDAN] Sir! Just wait a minute.

730
00:37:08,476 --> 00:37:10,311
Please don't disrespect our staff.

731
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:13,022
Hah. So I'm the disrespectful one here?

732
00:37:13,105 --> 00:37:16,943
Fine. I won't make a fuss
if you put my food on the house.

733
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:19,070
And give me a new plate of <i>sisig.</i>

734
00:37:19,153 --> 00:37:20,863
Wait a minute.

735
00:37:20,947 --> 00:37:23,658
You ordered a lot! You're scamming us!

736
00:37:23,741 --> 00:37:25,326
You're crazy.

737
00:37:25,409 --> 00:37:26,494
- [BLOW LANDS]
- Rain!

738
00:37:29,038 --> 00:37:30,373
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [CUSTOMER GRUNTS]

739
00:37:32,458 --> 00:37:35,127
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [CUSTOMER GROANING]

740
00:37:35,962 --> 00:37:37,088
You really don't want to stop?

741
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:40,424
- [CHAIR THUDS]
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]

742
00:37:42,385 --> 00:37:44,553
[CUSTOMER GROANING]

743
00:37:44,637 --> 00:37:47,765
We got you! But where did you get this?

744
00:37:47,848 --> 00:37:49,517
You don't even have hair on your head.

745
00:37:50,434 --> 00:37:52,270
Robbie, call the police.

746
00:37:52,353 --> 00:37:54,730
- [JORDAN] You okay?
- [RAIN] It hurts, boss.

747
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:56,232
[ROBBIE CHUCKLING]

748
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:58,985
- That was a bit wild.
- Well, he was big, boss!

749
00:37:59,068 --> 00:38:01,612
- I know.
- Right? Did you see his body?

750
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:03,072
I even hit him with a chair.

751
00:38:03,155 --> 00:38:05,574
- He didn't stop.
- He didn't stop.

752
00:38:05,658 --> 00:38:07,451
And then he wanted to punch me again!

753
00:38:07,535 --> 00:38:10,246
Yeah, I did see him going closer to you.

754
00:38:10,329 --> 00:38:12,331
Good thing the boss arrived.

755
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:14,458
While you were
just standing there earlier.

756
00:38:14,542 --> 00:38:15,668
Yeah.

757
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:18,421
- What did you do?
- Because I knew!

758
00:38:18,504 --> 00:38:20,214
- I knew you could handle him.
- Oh, wow.

759
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:22,383
I conceded because
I knew you could handle him.

760
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:23,676
Right?

761
00:38:24,343 --> 00:38:25,386
Listen.

762
00:38:26,012 --> 00:38:28,222
Our sales are still good,
although we're a mess.

763
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:29,598
That's true.

764
00:38:29,682 --> 00:38:35,479
[VALERIE BREATHING HEAVILY]

765
00:38:35,563 --> 00:38:36,939
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [ROBBIE] This one?

766
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:40,693
- Hi, babe.
- Hi, Jordan!

767
00:38:41,235 --> 00:38:42,903
I just finished working out.

768
00:38:42,987 --> 00:38:45,573
- Want to grab a midnight snack?
- Sorry, Val.

769
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:47,116
We're not done at the bar yet.

770
00:38:47,199 --> 00:38:48,492
We still have to check the inventory.

771
00:38:48,576 --> 00:38:51,370
Tomorrow, I promise.
I'll make it up to you.

772
00:38:51,954 --> 00:38:53,289
Okay, fine.

773
00:38:54,540 --> 00:38:55,583
Are you mad?

774
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:58,627
No. No, I'm fine.

775
00:38:58,711 --> 00:39:00,838
Anyway, I have to go now. Bye-bye.

776
00:39:00,921 --> 00:39:04,175
- [SIGHING DEEPLY]
- [GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

777
00:39:04,258 --> 00:39:05,634
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

778
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:08,471
[PHONE THUDS]

779
00:39:16,812 --> 00:39:18,647
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

780
00:39:20,483 --> 00:39:21,776
[BILLY] Yes, Auntie Pres. I just arrived.

781
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:23,944
- Good morning.
- Good morning, Ms. Billy.

782
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:26,655
Is Oliver's new glucose dosage
in the fridge?

783
00:39:26,739 --> 00:39:27,573
The one I prepared?

784
00:39:27,656 --> 00:39:29,367
Yes, I saw it.

785
00:39:29,450 --> 00:39:32,203
Please also check his
sugar level before bedtime,

786
00:39:32,286 --> 00:39:33,704
or if he looks weak.

787
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:34,997
If the low alarm goes off…

788
00:39:35,081 --> 00:39:36,207
- Good morning, ma'am!
- Morning.

789
00:39:36,290 --> 00:39:40,044
…that means he needs to eat,
even if it's just borderline.

790
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:41,504
- Good morning, chief!
- Good morning.

791
00:39:41,587 --> 00:39:43,130
E-signature, please.

792
00:39:44,673 --> 00:39:46,050
Oh, you'll do it upstairs.

793
00:39:46,133 --> 00:39:47,843
But talk to this baby boy.

794
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:50,805
He's been bugging me for a while now.

795
00:39:52,848 --> 00:39:53,682
<i>Oliver.</i>

796
00:39:53,766 --> 00:39:57,895
Yes, I told Auntie that
you'll be staying there.

797
00:39:57,978 --> 00:39:59,480
Don't be stubborn.

798
00:39:59,563 --> 00:40:02,400
But, Billy, we have an exam today!

799
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:04,318
<i>I already emailed your teacher earlier.</i>

800
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:07,154
You'll be given a make-up exam.

801
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:09,657
Didn't the doctor say you need to rest?

802
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:10,950
Don't be difficult, come on.

803
00:40:11,033 --> 00:40:14,120
When you return to school,
you'll be given a glucagon kit.

804
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:15,955
I already taught your teacher
how to use it.

805
00:40:16,038 --> 00:40:18,999
So during PE or any sports activity…?

806
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:22,920
<i>The insulin dose should be reduced,</i>
<i>and carbs increased.</i>

807
00:40:23,003 --> 00:40:24,839
<i>I already know that, Billy.</i>

808
00:40:24,922 --> 00:40:26,924
So when will I be going back to school?

809
00:40:27,007 --> 00:40:28,801
Tomorrow? The next day?

810
00:40:28,884 --> 00:40:31,345
Ssh. Shh, look at you.

811
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:32,346
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

812
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:35,015
He's so stubborn, right?
Don't think about it.

813
00:40:35,099 --> 00:40:40,104
It's better than forcing him
to go to school, right?

814
00:40:40,688 --> 00:40:44,066
Don't worry. I'm on leave until next week.
I'll take care of him.

815
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:46,235
N-Next week?!

816
00:40:46,318 --> 00:40:48,988
<i>So that means I won't be going</i>
<i>to school until next week?</i>

817
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:51,198
Biboy might end up
being the top of the class!

818
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:52,491
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

819
00:40:52,575 --> 00:40:54,702
Oh, see? He takes after someone I know!

820
00:40:54,785 --> 00:40:57,538
Hmph! Anyway, bye-bye.

821
00:40:57,621 --> 00:40:59,373
All right, Auntie Pres.
You're in charge of him.

822
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:01,959
Thank you. Bye, Oliver!

823
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:06,255
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

824
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:08,549
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

825
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:11,969
[BILLY] <i>LoveList knows that</i>
<i>love can get complicated.</i>

826
00:41:12,052 --> 00:41:15,306
<i>So after LoveSpeak, here comes LoveLine.</i>

827
00:41:15,389 --> 00:41:17,808
<i>Heartbroken? Confused?</i>

828
00:41:17,892 --> 00:41:21,187
<i>On LoveLine, you can talk</i>
<i>to real professionals</i>

829
00:41:21,270 --> 00:41:24,231
<i>who are always ready to guide</i>
<i>and listen to you.</i>

830
00:41:24,315 --> 00:41:25,691
<i>Real people.</i>

831
00:41:25,774 --> 00:41:27,026
<i>Real advice.</i>

832
00:41:27,109 --> 00:41:28,068
<i>Real love.</i>

833
00:41:29,236 --> 00:41:30,404
What do you guys think?

834
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:32,490
I feel like

835
00:41:32,573 --> 00:41:36,035
we need to visualize LoveLine more.

836
00:41:36,118 --> 00:41:40,080
Like, what it is. What it comes with.

837
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:44,126
Ah, do we have sample clips of our booths?

838
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,211
Even rough ideas?

839
00:41:45,294 --> 00:41:46,462
Do you have any?

840
00:41:47,338 --> 00:41:50,090
We can ask Jordan to build an AI model.

841
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:51,300
Yes.

842
00:41:51,383 --> 00:41:54,094
While waiting for LoveLine's
official launch, uh…

843
00:41:54,178 --> 00:41:57,014
we'll sustain teasers
on LoveList's socials.

844
00:41:57,097 --> 00:41:58,182
Mm-hmm.

845
00:41:58,265 --> 00:42:03,479
Billy, the cost of this rollout
is no joke.

846
00:42:03,562 --> 00:42:05,856
I'm already wearing these
wealth crystals every day.

847
00:42:05,940 --> 00:42:09,944
I don't even know where
to get the budget anymore.

848
00:42:10,027 --> 00:42:11,570
Yes, I know.

849
00:42:11,654 --> 00:42:15,491
Don't worry, I'll have a meeting
with a possible investor on Friday.

850
00:42:15,574 --> 00:42:17,243
What if…

851
00:42:17,326 --> 00:42:18,744
- No deal?
- Yeah.

852
00:42:18,827 --> 00:42:22,331
Well, I studied their company carefully.

853
00:42:22,414 --> 00:42:25,167
We seem to share the same core values.

854
00:42:25,251 --> 00:42:28,671
It looks like we're aligned
with their mission and vision.

855
00:42:28,754 --> 00:42:31,382
So, I think there will be a deal.

856
00:42:31,465 --> 00:42:33,133
I think. Let's claim it.

857
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:35,344
Miss, they're currently
in the middle of a meeting!

858
00:42:35,427 --> 00:42:37,513
Chief, I couldn't stop her.

859
00:42:37,596 --> 00:42:38,847
Billy, can we talk?

860
00:42:38,931 --> 00:42:43,269
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

861
00:42:43,352 --> 00:42:44,937
In private?

862
00:42:48,607 --> 00:42:49,900
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

863
00:42:50,568 --> 00:42:52,444
Ever since Jordan and I started dating,

864
00:42:52,528 --> 00:42:55,739
I've been helping you promote
LoveList for 11 months now.

865
00:42:56,323 --> 00:42:57,241
For free.

866
00:42:58,409 --> 00:43:02,830
So, it's my turn to ask for a favor.

867
00:43:02,913 --> 00:43:04,373
Of course.

868
00:43:05,708 --> 00:43:07,751
What do you need from me?

869
00:43:09,461 --> 00:43:10,754
[SIGHS]

870
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:14,008
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

871
00:43:14,091 --> 00:43:15,676
I want to propose to Jordan,

872
00:43:15,759 --> 00:43:17,720
and you're gonna help me set it up.

873
00:43:17,803 --> 00:43:23,058
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

874
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:24,143
Oh, wow.

875
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:26,353
Are you sure?

876
00:43:28,230 --> 00:43:29,273
I mean--

877
00:43:30,482 --> 00:43:32,860
Have you really thought this through?

878
00:43:34,111 --> 00:43:35,988
Didn't you just celebrate
your first anniversary?

879
00:43:36,071 --> 00:43:37,323
I think that's enough time for me

880
00:43:37,406 --> 00:43:39,950
to realize that
we're meant to be together.

881
00:43:40,034 --> 00:43:41,118
For good.

882
00:43:41,201 --> 00:43:42,536
[BILLY] Oh.

883
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:43,621
I want him.

884
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:50,419
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

885
00:43:55,132 --> 00:43:58,344
<i>I finally found my Prince Charming!</i>

886
00:43:58,427 --> 00:44:01,722
<i>I felt it wasn't my place to stop Val.</i>

887
00:44:01,805 --> 00:44:02,806
[JORDAN] <i>It's been years.</i>

888
00:44:02,890 --> 00:44:05,225
<i>There's still no update</i>
<i>about my mom's case.</i>

889
00:44:05,309 --> 00:44:06,393
[JUDE] <i>Who are you?</i>

890
00:44:06,477 --> 00:44:08,604
[NURSE] <i>I hope you never get tired of</i>
<i>taking care of your grandpa.</i>

891
00:44:08,687 --> 00:44:12,191
<i>Through this, you'll be able</i>
<i>to express yourself freely.</i>

892
00:44:12,274 --> 00:44:14,151
<i>Why are you painting a bird?</i>

893
00:44:14,234 --> 00:44:15,903
[ABI] <i>Because I want to be free.</i>

894
00:44:15,986 --> 00:44:17,738
<i>My father left us.</i>

895
00:44:17,821 --> 00:44:19,198
<i>So did my sibling.</i>

896
00:44:19,281 --> 00:44:21,659
[BILLY] <i>I just feel like</i>
<i>someone's watching me.</i>
